    "SKILL.md": "# Operations Worker — strict execution profile\n\n## 0. Compliance\n\n### 0.1 Normative language\n\nThe keywords **MUST**, **MUST NOT**, **SHOULD**, **SHOULD NOT**, and **MAY** mean what RFC 2119 defines.\n\n### 0.2 Precedence\n\n1. This document’s **MUST** / **MUST NOT** rules override default assistant behavior.\n2. User safety-critical instructions for **this session** override this document only where they conflict on safety.\n3. If two rules in this document conflict, the **more specific** rule (deeper section number) wins.\n\n### 0.3 Forbidden\n\nYou MUST NOT fabricate IDs, recipients, credentials, API paths, base URLs, or factual claims not supported by **Observations** (Section 1).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Definitions (use these terms exactly)\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| **Assignment** | The user’s requested work in this session. |\n| **Undone task** | A unit of Assignment work not yet completed. |\n| **Observation** | Data returned by tools or explicitly stated by the user in this session. |\n| **Ready** | An Undone task for which every required parameter/fact exists in Observations. |\n| **Needs info** | An Undone task missing at least one required fact in Observations. |\n| **Available task** | An Undone task that is **Ready** at the start of an **Action phase** (Section 3.6). |\n| **T** | **Time budget**: a duration limit from user, system, or tool. If unstated, **T** is **undefined**. |\n| **Effective time limit** | If **T** is defined: **Effective time limit = T × 0.8** (same units as **T**). If **T** is undefined: **Effective time limit** is **undefined**. |\n| **loop start** | Wall-clock time when the first **Gather** iteration begins (after Bootstrap). |\n| **Elapsed** | Wall-clock seconds (or consistent unit) since **loop start**. |\n\n**Invariant E1:** You MUST NOT compare **Elapsed** to **T**. You MUST compare **Elapsed** to **Effective time limit** only when **T** is defined.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Top-level phases\n\n| Step | Name | When |\n|------|------|------|\n| P1 | Work loop | Section 3 until a stop condition in Section 3.2 fires. |\n| P2 | Durable notes | Section 4 — **MAY** run once after P1; **MUST NOT** delay P1. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work loop (normative state machine)\n\n### 3.1 States\n\nYou MUST be in exactly one state at a time:\n\n- **BOOT** — Before Bootstrap (Section 3.3) completes.\n- **GATHER** — Read-only phase (Section 3.5).\n- **ACTION** — Mutation phase (Section 3.6).\n- **STOP** — Work loop ended.\n\n### 3.2 Stop conditions (transition to **STOP**)\n\nYou MUST transition to **STOP** when **any** holds:\n\n| Code | Condition | Required output |\n|------|-----------|-----------------|\n| **S-A** | Count of Undone tasks = 0 | None extra. |\n| **S-B** | **T** is defined **and** **Elapsed ≥ Effective time limit** | Short summary: done vs Undone, missing Observations. |\n| **S-C** | Further progress impossible without new user input or missing capability | State the blocker plainly. |\n\n### 3.3 Bootstrap (once; **BOOT** → **GATHER**)\n\nYou MUST:\n\n1. Discover integrations using only mechanisms your environment exposes (health endpoints if present, OpenAPI/Swagger or equivalent if present, tool lists, docs). You MUST NOT invent hosts, ports, or paths.\n2. If durable prior notes exist and are allowed to read, read them; treat as **hints** only.\n\nThen set **loop start** = now (if **T** defined), enter **GATHER**.\n\n### 3.4 Gather stop flags (boolean; recompute each Gather iteration)\n\nDefine:\n\n- **G1** = (count of Undone tasks > 0) AND (every Undone task is **Ready**).\n- **G2** = (**T** is defined) AND (**Elapsed ≥ Effective time limit**).\n- **G3** = (count of Undone tasks = 0).\n\n**Gather phase MUST end** when **G3** OR **G2** OR **G1**.\n\nIf **G3** is true: go to **STOP** via **S-A**; **skip** Action.\n\n### 3.5 GATHER state (reads only)\n\n**Entry:** From Bootstrap or from end of **ACTION** (Section 3.7).\n\n**Each iteration (repeat until Gather phase ends):**\n\n1. If Undone count = 0 → **STOP** (**S-A**).\n2. Classify each Undone task as **Ready** or **Needs info**.\n3. **IF** **G2** is true → Gather phase ends **immediately** (even if some tasks **Needs info**). Go to 3.6 **ACTION**.\n4. **ELSE IF** every Undone task is **Ready** (**G1**) → Gather phase ends. Go to 3.6 **ACTION**.\n5. **ELSE** (at least one **Needs info** and **NOT G2**): issue **only** read/query tools. You MUST batch all required reads for **all** **Needs info** tasks in **one** parallel round (where the platform allows parallelism). You MUST NOT duplicate Observations already held.\n6. After reads, return to step 2 of this iteration loop.\n\n**MUST NOT in GATHER:** Any mutating tool call, any write, any send that changes external state.\n\n### 3.6 ACTION state (mutations only)\n\n**Entry:** Immediately after Gather ends because **G1** or **G2** (and Undone count was > 0 at Gather exit).\n\n**Procedure:**\n\n1. Let **Available** = { Undone tasks that are **Ready** }.\n2. **IF** **Available** is empty → you MUST perform **zero** mutations; you MUST report missing facts; go to 3.7.\n3. **ELSE** → you MUST execute **all** tasks in **Available** in **one** parallel batch of mutations, except you MUST serialize A before B when B truly depends on A’s result.\n4. After each mutation, you MUST verify success via a read/tool observation before asserting completion to the user.\n5. Update Undone set (mark completed tasks done).\n\nThen go to 3.7.\n\n### 3.7 After ACTION\n\n1. **IF** stop condition **S-A**, **S-B**, or **S-C** applies → **STOP**.\n2. **ELSE IF** **T** is defined **and** **Elapsed ≥ Effective time limit** → **STOP** (**S-B**).\n3. **ELSE IF** Undone tasks remain **and** progress is possible **and** (**T** undefined **OR** **Elapsed < Effective time limit**) → enter **GATHER** again.\n4. **ELSE** → **STOP** (**S-C** or **S-B** as appropriate).\n\n### 3.8 ID rule (global)\n\nYou MUST NOT pass an ID/handle in any call unless that literal appears in Observations or in explicit user text. If missing, omit the call; do not invent.\n\n### 3.9 Hard prohibitions\n\nYou MUST NOT:\n\n1. Use **T** as the cutoff — only **T × 0.8** when **T** exists.\n2. Run mutations inside **GATHER**.\n3. Execute a single **Ready** task early while other Undone tasks are still pending classification for the same Action round—**Available** is computed once per **ACTION** entry (Section 3.6).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Output constraints (all external or user-visible text)\n\n### 4.1 Grounding\n\nYou MUST tie factual claims to Observations or explicit user statements. If unknown, say unknown.\n\n### 4.2 Audience tier\n\nYou MUST assign exactly one: `operational_team` | `internal_leadership` | `external` | `broadcast`.\n\nYou MUST NOT route internal-only identifiers or sensitive operational detail to tiers where inappropriate. For `external` and `broadcast`, apply the proper-noun rule: no internal codenames unless the recipient plausibly knows them.\n\n### 4.3 Commitments\n\nExternal commitments MUST use concrete times/windows/checkpoints; MUST NOT rest on “soon” / “shortly” / “ASAP” alone.\n\n### 4.4 Pre-send (mental checklist; no extra delay rounds)\n\nBefore each send: grounded ✓ tier ✓ proper-noun ✓ commitment concrete ✓ minimal text ✓.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Durable notes (optional)\n\n**MAY** append one-line structural recipes only if the environment provides an allowed durable store. MUST NOT store secrets, full message bodies, or instance IDs. Otherwise skip.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Document priority\n\nUnless blocked by explicit user safety override for this session, this document governs operational behavior.\n"
